WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
In the year 1405, Zheng He set out leading a huge fleet.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
The dock was crowded with people, and sailors were busy loading goods onto the great ships.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The giant treasure ships raised their red sails and sailed toward the vast, boundless ocean.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The fleet moved slowly forward across the sea in neat formation.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The fleet reached Southeast Asia and South Asia, where it exchanged friendly visits with people of many countries.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
People at the ports waved in welcome, and children looked curiously at the tall treasure ships.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
They carried out trade and exchanges, and brought back precious spices and treasures.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
The markets were bustling, with all kinds of spices and gems sparkling brightly.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Over twenty-eight years, Zheng He completed seven great voyages in all.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The giraffe brought back by the fleet drew curious crowds in the capital.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The story of Zheng He's voyages to the Western Ocean linked China with the Indian Ocean world.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
People stood on the shore waving, welcoming the heroes home safely.
